      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Transformers - kVA Ratings vs. Volt and Amps\n\nA transformer transfers electrical energy from one circuit to another through inductively coupled conductors. For an ideal transformer:\n\n**U1 / U2 = N1 / N2 = I2 / I1**\n\nWhere:\n- U = electrical potential difference (Voltage)\n- N = number of turns of wire\n- I = current (Amps)\n\n### Example\nA transformer with 500 primary turns, 3000 secondary turns and 230 V primary voltage:\n\nU2 = U1 × N2 / N1 = 230 × 3000 / 500 = 1380 V = 1.38 kV"
    },
